@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;performance] world-import-preserves-reuse-evidence
A normal world import MUST NOT delete its receiving namespace before current source,
settings and native validation can decide per-package reuse. Existing or unknown assets
MUST NOT be mistaken for certified current outputs merely because they are preserved.
Retirement MUST be restricted to an explicit owning producer's complete known obsolete
membership after successful replacement validation and external-reference preflight.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] repeatable-owned-world-map
World assembly MUST populate a fresh unsaved Slice world before saving it to its
owned map path, including when that map already exists. It MUST NOT delete the
receiving asset namespace or ignore blank-world/save failure. Successful completion
MUST require the actual populated world's save result; engine save is not an atomic
preservation guarantee for a previous map on failure.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] english-user-facing-text
The game is in English. Every user-facing string in Python, C++, runtime data and UI
(including station and terminal names, signs, timetables, arrival boards, broadcasts,
map zones, hints and HUD prompts) MUST be natural English and MUST NOT contain French
words or French labels. Proper-noun world toponyms that are not French words MAY remain.
